# Prada L'Homme Intense — Z2 computational selection

Date: 2026-09-05. Immediate recipe parent: PLI-ZERO-ASTRA-Z1.
Authority: user asked to execute the computational-finalization proposal.
Mode: COMPUTATIONAL_PERFUMERY_ONLY; one final complete blend for later testing.

## Scope and boundary

Select one complete target-linked iris/amber/patchouli/sandalwood/tonka composition.
All interim comparisons are virtual; no physical omissions, A/B samples, preparatory
smell trials or purchases are requested. Sensory, safety and physical-release
authority remain separate. No new pipeline scripts, engine patches, inventory
changes, authority-pin edits, external model providers or Git integration.
Preserve Z1 and all earlier artifacts as lineage. Use existing APIs in bounded
inline calculations; retain inputs, commands, hashes and numerical results.

## Ordered work

1. Recheck inventory, source provenance, mass/stock accounting and model contracts.
2. Build a mass-faithful common-matrix comparison using Z1's 17 selected products.
   Investigate 243 combinations of five composition axes, not a material-count
   objective: subject versus floral/woody space; sandalwood versus cedar grain;
   sandalwood body versus accent; tonka warmth versus patchouli/amber contrast;
   almond-powder junction versus floral iris. Each retains 1000 product parts.
3. Compare selected virtual omissions and role-matched alternatives (Bacdanol,
   Javanol, Beta Ionone) inside the full mixture. Declare removed active loading
   and carrier changes; an omission is not an otherwise identical matrix.
4. Refine a bounded shortlist. Examine per-material headspace/OAV and the existing
   five-window uncalibrated temporal model. Do not convert these into perceived
   contribution, sensory depth, liking, or a single aesthetic score.
5. Repeat decision-relevant cases with isolated source-informed MW/VP inputs,
   temperature and explicit ODT/activity-model stress hypotheses. Stress factors
   are not measured uncertainty distributions or confidence intervals. Unknown
   constituent properties remain unknown; natural composite coverage stays visible.
6. Select one complete candidate using the target hierarchy, differentiated roles,
   defensible tradeoffs, numerical robustness and stock feasibility. Prefer a
   moderate allocation when numerical alternatives do not establish a useful
   distinction. Preserve unsupported blending roles as hypotheses, not proven
   synergy or automatic pruning instructions.
7. Produce one canonical selection accounting record, readable formula and mass
   card. Re-evaluate its actual declared stock-carrier scenario and run one final
   integrated diagnostic with the immediate Z1 parent. Present the required full
   formatter output in chat and append it verbatim to the formula.
8. Verify exact totals, ppm, carrier closure, parent-dose changes, case counts,
   replay consistency, report binding and preservation of earlier bytes. Use
   focused existing tests; do not claim release-level project verification.

## Predeclared decision principles

- Iris is the subject; woods, patchouli, amber and tonka have connected but
  differentiated functions. No generic base-Prada gate may redefine Intense.
- Lower modelled almond-powder crowding is a screening preference, not proof of
  improved smell. It cannot alone select a formula when its ODT is unverified.
- Neither higher total OAV nor more materials is a selection objective.
- A material may contribute to a blend without being individually identifiable.
  Existing headspace APIs cannot prove such configurational contributions.
- Compare model alarms as a vector and keep the final composition judgment
  explicit. No fabricated calibrated complexity/liking/similarity score.
- Do not require preliminary physical evidence to select the computational final.
  Do not claim sensory success, global optimality, solubility or safety afterward.

## Stopping rule

Freeze one candidate after the declared comparison set and focused refinement,
when the remaining composition choices have explicit reasons and uncertainties
do not invalidate those reasons. Where the model cannot choose, disclose the
parent's formulation judgment and its limits rather than inventing evidence.
The final state is COMPUTATIONALLY_SELECTED, with physical release HOLD.
